# 
# https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/characteristic
<https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/characteristic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/characteristic> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentProperty> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/characteristic> .
<https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/characteristic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty> .
<https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/characteristic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The object property characteristic indicates a relationship between a Materials Library, Sample or Measurement Area and anything that further describes it in the RDMS.\n\nThis can be the result of applying an actual characterization technique on a sample (e.g., the results of TEM, EDX...), or associating it with miscellaneous file uploads (photos, documents...). A Measurement Area can also contain characteristics, such as individual EDX composition results.\n\nThe entity pointed by at by this property may contain metadata such as creators and dates, whose raw values (e.g. file paths or composition values) can be accessed by the crc:value property" .
