<https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/substep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The substep object property is used to indicate a part of a step in a handover workflow that has been broken into smaller (sub)steps. This is also employed in handover workflow models.\n\nMore specifically, in a handover workflow, this is employed by Handover Groups to point to the start of the chain of handovers that they represent, and by an inidividual Handover to point to the individual characterization activities that happened inside it." .
<https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/substep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "substep" .
